{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat docs/architecture/ui-v2/DESIGN-V2.md docs/architecture/ui-v2/invariants.md docs/architecture/ui-v2/state-ownership.md docs/architecture/ui-v2/screens/inbox-reads.md docs/architecture/ui-v2/screens/shell.md'","aggregated_output":"# UI v2 \"Refined Native\" — design specification\n\nStatus: C27 deliverable, reviewed at the 9/10 bar (D058). This document and\nits companions ([tokens](tokens.md), [state ownership](state-ownership.md),\n[invariants](invariants.md), [screens](screens/), [provenance](provenance.md))\nare what every P09 chunk is judged against. The existing\n[DESIGN.md](../DESIGN.md) remains authoritative for the native authority\ninterface, transport, Academy presentation ownership and the Harness; this\ndocument changes only how the desktop presents those.\n\n## 1. Scope and deliverable\n\nThe reviewed prototype is extracted in three layers, in order:\n\n1. **Spec** (C27, this folder): tokens, screen inventory, state ownership,\n   invariants, interaction contracts, copy, provenance, acceptance criteria.\n2. **TypeScript presentation** (C28–C29, then per-destination chunks): the new\n   shell and screens in `apps/desktop`, built against wire fixtures and the\n   mock runtime, behind a Rust-owned `ui_variant` flag.\n3. **Rust contract** (within each destination chunk): the intents, scopes and\n   refusals the screens need, implemented over existing desktop-core services\n   and exported through ts-rs.\n\nThe first implementation slice is the shell plus the first-run wizard and\nadd-tenant sheet (C28–C29). Harness, Inbox/reads, reviews/Administration, API\nClient, Test Cases and the Academy embed follow (C30–C34). The legacy shell,\nits feature-view switch, the flag and the legacy native acceptance scripts are\nremoved in C34; the phase is not complete while any destination renders only\nin the legacy shell.\n\n## 2. Frozen reference\n\nCanvas https://claude.ai/artifact/2SEXT1XMHdZkxHvdw8oaYL, page \"Refined Native\nv2\", version 134. The six R2 files are copied verbatim under\n[prototype/](prototype/) with SHA-256 hashes in `MANIFEST.sha256`. They are\nimmutable inputs. Codex scored the prototype 8/10 on rounds 4–16; the five\nopen round-16 items are carried as known gaps (§10) and closed in\nimplementation, not by further prototype rounds.\n\n## 3. Architecture fit\n\n- **Authority** stays with desktop-core (D014). The UI dispatches intents and\n  observes scopes through the existing two-command Tauri bridge. Every\n  prototype state field is assigned in [state-ownership.md](state-ownership.md);\n  no persisted or tenant-sensitive state is UI-owned (UI state is transient\n  presentation state only), and no state goes to browser storage.\n- **Contract**: new intents, scopes and refusals are Rust types with ts-rs\n  derives, regenerated by `xtask bindings`. A hand-written parser is added to\n  the contracts client only where runtime validation beyond the type is needed.\n- **Shell flag**: `ShellSnapshot.ui_variant` (`legacy` | `v2`) and\n  `ShellSnapshot.onboarding` (`needed` | `inProgress` | `done`) are Rust-owned,\n  fixture-able and seedable by native acceptance. The React root switches on\n  them.\n- **Navigation inventory**: one Rust list (feature ids with availability,\n  label, shortcut index and sidebar membership) feeds the native menu, the\n  sidebar and the command palette. Feature ids gain `home` and `inbox`;\n  `library` is shown as \"Test Cases\"; `gateway` and `redTeam` render inside\n  Administration's accordion; `sessions`, `import` and `settings` stay\n  reachable from the palette and Administration.\n- **Shortcuts** ⌘1–⌘9 are defined by the native menu, which dispatches\n  `navigate`; the sidebar displays the menu's truth.\n- **Transient state**: a small zustand store per screen family (shell, wizard,\n  inbox, admin, harness, workbench); React state only for form fields.\n- **Tokens**: local `--v2-*` custom properties ([tokens.md](tokens.md));\n  Academy variables untouched for the embedded learner view.\n- **Copy**: one `copy.ts` per screen family exporting constants; tests assert\n  exact strings. The voice is the wizard's: this app is built entirely on\n  Palo Alto Networks' public APIs and exists to show application builders what\n  those interfaces make possible; it explains the API call as you go.\n- **Show the calls**: a Rust-owned preference reveals, for each action, the\n  request and response as the diagnostics module already redacts them\n  (credential ids in place of secrets, a note that the core attaches the real\n  header). Default on until onboarding completes.\n\n## 4. Layout rhythm\n\nShared by every destination, the wizard and the add-tenant sheet:\n\n- 32px top and 44px side page margins; 26px/700 titles; 18–20px card\n  padding; 10–12px gaps; 32px controls; 14px body, 12px secondary (11px only\n  pills, eyebrows and mono badges); 860px reading cap; 244px rail (first-run\n  wizard rail 320px).\n- Minimum window 1180×720. Below 1280 wide the rail collapses to icons with\n  tooltips; nothing scrolls horizontally.\n- Tool workspaces (Harness, API Client) have a title row like every other\n  destination; no destination is exempt from the rhythm.\n\n## 5. Destinations\n\n| Sidebar | Feature id | Shortcut | Contract |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Home | `home` (new) | ⌘1 | [screens/shell.md](screens/shell.md) |\n| Inbox | `inbox` (new) | ⌘2 | [screens/inbox-reads.md](screens/inbox-reads.md) |\n| Harness | `harness` | ⌘3 | [screens/harness.md](screens/harness.md) |\n| Academy | `academy` | ⌘4 | [screens/academy.md](screens/academy.md) |\n| Test Cases | `library` | ⌘5 | [screens/api-client-test-cases.md](screens/api-client-test-cases.md) |\n| API Client | `apiClient` | ⌘6 | same |\n| Administration | `administration` (+ `gateway`, `redTeam` inside) | ⌘7 | [screens/reviews-administration.md](screens/reviews-administration.md) |\n| Tenant switcher | — | ⌘T | [screens/shell.md](screens/shell.md) |\n| Command palette | — | ⌘K | same |\n| First-run wizard, add-tenant sheet | — | — | [screens/wizard.md](screens/wizard.md) |\n\nRed Team is read-only everywhere. Gamification appears only inside the Academy\nembed. Product availability is governed by §6.\n\n## 6. Products, admitted services and the unsupported boundary\n\nThe prototype shows six products. Only a product with an admitted service in\ndesktop-core is verified, inventoried or changed; the rest render as\nunavailable. Nothing in P09 adds a product API.\n\n| Product | Admitted reads | Admitted changes | P09 treatment |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| AI Runtime Security | `ManagementResource` (profiles, topics, applications, API keys, deployment profiles, DLP catalog/profiles/patterns, filtering profiles, dictionaries, sessions); scan (`scan.rs`) | `ChangeKind` Profiles, Topics, Applications, ApiKeys, DataPatterns, DataProfiles, FilteringProfiles, Dictionaries with `ChangeAction` Create/Version/Rotate/Delete/… (`changes.rs`) | Full: Administration tabs, reviews, Playground, Inbox items |\n| AI Gateway | `GatewayRead` (inventory, detail, integration models, prerequisites, observe, MCP servers) | Gateway `ChangeKind`s (workspaces, providers, routes, guardrails, service/user keys, integrations) | Full, inside Administration; Harness lifecycle 2 reads `McpServers` |\n| AI Red Teaming | `red_team.rs` reads (scan inventory, statistics, static reports; C13) | none (execution stays a disabled preview) | Read-only card and tabs; Test Cases \"Inspect\" only |\n| Model/skill observability (AI Supply Chain in the prototype) | C13 model/skill reads | none | Read-only; shown under its C13 name, never as a scanning product |\n| Agentic Identity Security | none | none | **Not available in this release**: card and accordion entry with the dependency gate (\"needs an admitted AIS service; see D058\"); not selectable in the wizard; never verified; no inventory, no policy review |\n| Agentic Endpoint Security | none | none | Same as AIS; the prototype's AES policy review, discovered-AI table and warning demo are fixtures only and are not implemented |\n\nThe per-tab and per-action mapping, including the restricted Runtime and\nGateway change matrices (for example no application Create, no API-key\nUpdate, no data-profile Delete) and every removed or unavailable prototype\ntab, is enumerated in\n[screens/administration-inventory.md](screens/administration-inventory.md).\n\nRules: an unavailable product or tab never produces a verification result, an\nInbox item, an inventory row or a review. The wizard's verify step lists it\nas \"Not available\" (not pass, warning or fail). Test V2-T19 asserts that the\nadmin inventory for an unavailable product has no tabs and no actions, and\nV2-R10 asserts that no intent exists that would mutate it; V2-T20 and V2-R11\ncover unavailable tabs and denied actions within admitted products.\n\n## 7. Error presentation\n\n- **Refusal** (core refused an intent): warn toast with the refusal reason and\n  the tenant named; never a modal. Guard-type refusals (tenant switch with a\n  pending decision) render their dialog from the refusal payload.\n- **Delivery unknown**: inline \"not confirmed\" state on the control that\n  dispatched, with Retry; the control is not reset.\n- **Contract violation**: generic warn toast; detail to diagnostics.\n\n## 8. Accessibility additions\n\nThe native acceptance checklist gains four items that every P09 chunk's\nacceptance script asserts: accent-colour focus ring on every focusable\ncontrol (inset variant where declared); `role=\"status\"` live regions for read\nstatus, API send completion and review apply; one topmost modal with\n`aria-hidden` siblings and focus return; toasts persist under Reduce Motion.\nExisting requirements (keyboard-only, VoiceOver attributes, 150%/200% zoom,\ncontrast AA) continue to apply to every changed screen.\n\n## 9. Budgets\n\nExisting `budgets.json` entries carry unchanged. New: a tenant switch renders\nthe new tenant's Home from cached scopes within 100 ms, with read status\nshowing pending until the read lands (measured by the C30 workload).\n\n## 10. Known gaps carried from the prototype\n\nCodex round 16 (score 8) left five items, closed by the chunk named:\n\n1. Secret disclosure survives a tenant switch with the key review open → I6, C31.\n2. Applied injection-override examples show \"Not demonstrated\" → topic\n   verdicts keyed separately from detectors, profile-aware, C31.\n3. Administration creation labels from a per-product single value → per-tab\n   `AdminInventory` capability and label, C31.\n4. Home snooze tooltip hard-codes \"Snooze 24 hours\" → shared item\n   `snoozeLabel`, I11, C30.\n5. API Client Send announces nothing → `role=\"status\"` completion region, C33.\n\n## 11. Verification\n\n- Behaviour: Vitest + Testing Library component tests, one named fixture per\n  prototype wrapper board; the board → initial props → test id table is in\n  [screens/boards.md](screens/boards.md), so reviewed-state coverage can be\n  audited without reconstructing canvas wrappers.\n- Contract: Rust integration tests per invariant (`V2-Rxx`).\n- Native: the existing Accessibility-API scripts, extended per chunk, plus a\n  screenshot evidence set per chunk at 100% and 200% zoom in both themes filed\n  under `evidence/Cxx/screens/`.\n- Live: only C29 (wizard verify against Vulture, reads only) and C31 (review\n  apply against Redtail under the `airs-v2-c25-` prefix) run live, inside the\n  scope the owner designated on 2026-10-25. Every other chunk runs on fixtures\n  and the mock runtime.\n- Review: C27 at 9/10 in every dimension, enforced by the controller (a\n  `docs_only` chunk refuses owner acceptance and needs no native\n  preparation); C28–C34 may complete at 8 under D034 and are raised to 9\n  before the P09 phase review.\n- Legacy native scripts removed in C34 are first mapped, assertion by\n  assertion, to replacement native-check ids (C34 milestone 2), so the\n  cumulative P09 gate keeps exercising every earlier authority and\n  accessibility requirement.\n# Normative invariants\n\nThese twelve rules are the behaviours Codex forced into the prototype over\nsixteen review rounds. They are normative: an implementation chunk that\nviolates one fails its behaviour or authority dimension regardless of how the\nscreen looks. Code shape is free; the rule and its test are not.\n\nEach rule names its acceptance test id. `V2-Txx` tests are Vitest component\ntests in the desktop app (fixture-driven); `V2-Rxx` are Rust integration tests\nin desktop-core; `V2-Nxx` are native acceptance checks added to\n`native-checks.json` by the chunk that implements the rule.\n\n| Id | Rule | Tests | Chunk |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| I1 | There is exactly one tenant-switch path. The core refuses a switch while a Harness decision is pending; the UI renders the archive-or-discard guard from the refusal and re-dispatches with the chosen resolution. | V2-R01 refusal on pending decision; V2-T01 guard rendered from refusal payload; V2-N01 switch via switcher, palette and menu all pass through the guard | C30 |\n| I2 | Every observed scope is per tenant. Switching tenants never shows another tenant's Inbox items, reads, reviews, conversations, drafts or rotation state. | V2-R02 scope isolation across two tenants; V2-T02 switcher round-trip leaves per-tenant transient state intact | C30 |\n| I3 | A review is bound to the tenant and resource it was opened for and applies only when the typed name matches, validated in the core. A tenant change invalidates the review. | V2-R03 confirmReview refuses on mismatch and on changed context; V2-T03 Apply disabled until names match | C31 |\n| I4 | Reads are finite. The UI distinguishes \"first read pending\" from \"no activity\", reports per-product partial coverage, and the completion toast is warn-kind whenever any source is partial. | V2-R04 ReadStatus transitions; V2-T04 toast kind and text per coverage; V2-N02 pending state visible on first run | C30 |\n| I5 | API responses are immutable snapshots. A later configuration change never alters an earlier response in history; a newly sent request reflects the change. | V2-R05 history entries hash-stable; V2-T05 topic applied → old response unchanged, new response includes it | C33 |\n| I6 | An issued secret is disclosed only through the host (`RevealSecret` sheet, host clipboard), is held per result for the active context and never persisted; any review exit, including a tenant switch or context retirement, drops it (`ForgetSecret`) and resets the reveal state. A dropped secret is not recoverable; the UI offers to issue another key. | V2-R06 held key dropped on review exit, switch and retirement; Reveal after drop refuses; V2-T06 resumed rotation shows no secret controls | C31 |\n| I7 | Key rotation is the admitted sequence additional key (`Version`) → local deployment acknowledgement → old key `Delete` with readback. Until the old key is removed, the reminder is a distinct Inbox item with its own identity and stated return time and the key table shows both keys. Two timestamps are stored once and labelled distinctly: deployment acknowledged (local statement) and old key removed (remote readback). A failed or unknown issuance never reissues automatically; a rejected or unknown Delete keeps the reminder and leaves the completion timestamp unset; unknown outcomes are shown as unconfirmed with reconciliation, never as complete. | V2-R07 state machine incl. failed/unknown issuance and rejected/unknown delete; V2-T07 Inbox item lifecycle; V2-T08 timestamps labelled and stable after refresh | C31 |\n| I8 | One topmost modal. Siblings of the topmost dialog are `aria-hidden`; Escape closes only the topmost; focus returns to the opener. | V2-T09 stacking; V2-N03 keyboard-only dialog traversal | C28 |\n| I9 | A verdict or severity is colour plus icon plus word, never colour alone. | V2-T10 every verdict renderer emits all three; V2-N04 accessibility tree carries the word | C28 |\n| I10 | Toasts have a kind (ok, info, warn), expire on a timer, and are presentation only: everything a toast says is derivable from an observed scope. With Reduce Motion on, toasts persist until dismissed. | V2-T11 kinds and expiry; V2-N05 Reduce Motion persistence | C28 |\n| I11 | Inbox acknowledge and snooze are per item, core-owned, with the return time stated wherever the action is offered (Home, Inbox row, Inbox detail) and identical across them. | V2-R08 snooze return computed in core; V2-T12 Home and Inbox labels equal | C30 |\n| I12 | A fresh tenant never shows seeded or sample data. Its first Harness send creates a user conversation; its Inbox is empty until the first read lands. | V2-R09 fresh tenant scopes empty; V2-T13 first send creates conversation | C30, C32 |\n\nRules I1, I3, I6 and I7 are authority rules under D014: the core owns the\ndecision, the UI renders it. No invariant may be satisfied by invented data: a\nproduct, tab or operation without an admitted service renders as unavailable\n(DESIGN-V2 §6), and a test that passes only on fixtures for such a capability\nis a specification defect.\n# State ownership\n\nEvery state key the frozen prototype actually holds is listed here, by file\nand by the name the prototype uses, with its owner, where it lives, its\nlifetime, and whether the implementation keeps, renames, derives or drops it.\n\n- **Core** — Rust-owned in desktop-core, exposed through `observe`\n  (persisted in the store or session-held), never in browser storage.\n- **UI** — transient presentation state in a per-screen-family zustand store\n  (shell, wizard, inbox, admin, harness, workbench) or React form state.\n  Lost on reload by design.\n- **Host** — never leaves the native host (secret sheet, clipboard).\n- **Dropped** — not implemented; the reason is in [provenance.md](provenance.md).\n\nThe inventory was produced from `grep -o` over `s.*`, `ts.*` and `f.*` in\n`prototype/R2App.dc.html` and `prototype/R2Onboard.dc.html` (version 134)\nand reconciled by hand; a key missing here is a specification defect.\n\n## R2Onboard — wizard and add-tenant sheet (`s.*`, `s.f.*`)\n\n| Prototype key | Meaning | Owner | Where / intent | Lifetime | Disposition |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `s.idx`, `s.path`, `s.vi` | current step, step path, visited steps | UI | wizard store | until the wizard closes | kept; `onboarding=inProgress` is set in core when the welcome step is left |\n| `s.f.name` | tenant display name | UI → Core | `completeOnboarding`/`addTenant` | written at completion | kept |\n| `s.env`, `s.region` | environment, region selects | UI → Core | same | same | kept |\n| `s.f.tsg` | TSG id (10 digits) | UI → Core | same | same | kept |\n| `s.f.clientId`, `s.f.secret` | management OAuth client id and secret (required in the prototype) | id: UI → Core; secret: **Host** | id in `addTenant`; secret entered only in the host secret sheet, vault record id returned | secret never in the web layer | **changed** (deviation P17): management credentials become an optional second section under D013; the id is kept, the secret field is replaced by \"Add management client…\" |\n| `s.scanOn`, `s.f.scanKey` | scan key toggle and value | toggle: UI; key: **Host** | \"Add scan key…\" opens the host secret sheet; required for first run (D013) | never in the web layer | **changed** (P1, P17): toggle removed on first run (the scan key is required); kept in add mode |\n| `s.gwOn`, `s.f.ws`, `s.f.endpoint`, `s.f.gwKey` | Gateway section toggle, workspace name, endpoint URL, workspace key | toggle/ws/endpoint: UI → Core; key: **Host** | `addTenant.gateway{ws, endpoint}`; key via secret sheet | — | kept; key path changed (P1) |\n| `s.tried`, `s.vsig`, `s.vsStale` | validation attempted, validation signature, stale flag | UI (tried) / Core (signature, stale) | wizard component; `setup.verify.stale`, `setup.completable` | per step / per draft | kept; the signature and the completion gate moved to the core so the presentation cannot complete over stale results |\n| `s.vs` | verify results per product | Core | `ShellSnapshot.setup.verify` (streamed `VerifyStep`s from `verifyTenantSetup`, with `done`/`failed`/`stale`) | until the draft completes or is discarded | kept; computed in core, including staleness against a signature of the draft's inputs |\n| `s.aesFixed`, `s.failCleared` | AES warning demo acknowledged; failed row cleared | UI | wizard store | per run | **changed**: AES is not an admitted product (P18); the warning demo becomes a generic \"warning row\" fixture on an admitted product |\n| `s.prods` | selected products | UI → Core | `completeOnboarding.products` | written at completion | kept; unavailable products are not selectable (P18) |\n| `s.packs`, `s.casesState` | starter packs selected, pack state | UI → Core | `completeTenantSetup.products` → the bundled catalog's cases as library entries named by their starter pack, Not run (P55) | written at completion | kept |\n| `s.acad`, `s.af` (`f.email`, `f.dname`), `s.streaks`, `s.remind` | local Academy account form, streaks, reminders | **Dropped** / Core (Academy) | Academy identity is hosted (D004–D006, C04); the step signs in or skips | — | **changed** (P19): no local account, streaks or reminders in the wizard |\n| `s.help` | help popover open | UI | wizard store | transient | kept |\n| `s.opened` | \"Open Prisma AIRS\" progress | UI | mirrors the `onboarding` transition | transient | kept |\n| `s.theme` | theme prop | Core | `appearance` | — | kept (observed) |\n\n## R2App — shell (`s.*`)\n\n| Prototype key | Meaning | Owner | Where | Lifetime | Disposition |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `s.tenant`, `s.byTenant` | active tenant; per-tenant state bag | Core | `ShellSnapshot.active`, per-tenant scopes below | persisted | kept; the bag is replaced by scopes |\n| `s.screen` | destination | Core | `navigate` intent, `ShellSnapshot.features` | session | kept; feature ids gain `home`, `inbox` |\n| `s.theme` | theme | Core | `appearance` | persisted | kept |\n| `s.wizard`, `s.added` | first-run wizard open; add-tenant sheet result | Core / UI | `ShellSnapshot.onboarding`; sheet result is a toast | — | kept |\n| `s.overlayDone` | prototype overlay bookkeeping | **Dropped** | canvas-only | — | dropped |\n| `s.palette`, `s.pq` | palette open, query | UI | shell store | transient | kept |\n| `s.tenantOpen`, `s.guard` | switcher open; switch guard | UI | shell store; guard content from the `SwitchBlocked` refusal (`to`, `pending`, `completion`), rendered by the shell for a switch and by the wizard for a setup completion | transient | kept (I1); completion is the same guarded path (P36) |\n| `s.toast`, `s.toastKind`, `s.undo` | toast text, kind, undo target | UI | shell store, timer | ≤ 6 s | kept (I10) |\n| `s.detail`, `s.sheet` | detail sheet; confirm sheet | UI | shell store modal stack | transient | kept (I8) |\n| `s.explain` | explain-mode toggle | UI | shell store | transient | kept |\n| `s.sel`, `s.itab` | Inbox selection, tab | UI | shell store, keyed by tenant id | transient; a switch round trip keeps it (I2) | kept |\n| `s.product`, `s.exp`, `s.ptab`, `s.allOpen`, `s.adminNav`, `s.adminQ`, `s.tree` | Administration product, expanded set, tab per product, expand-all, nav mode, search, tree | UI | admin store | transient | kept |\n| `s.review`, `s.reviewKind`, `s.reviewFrom`, `s.reviewTenant`, `s.reviewApplied` | review open, kind, origin, bound tenant, applied | Core | `Review` scope (tenant-bound, invalidated on context change) | session | kept; the UI holds only \"open\" |\n| `s.typed` | typed confirmation | UI | admin store | until review exit | kept (I3) |\n| `s.secretVisible` | reveal toggle | **Host** | `RevealSecret` sheet; UI holds nothing | 60 s sheet | **changed** (P2): no web reveal state |\n| `s.credOpen`, `s.credVal` | credential dialog open, value | Host | credential entry is the host secret sheet | — | **changed** (P1): no web credential value |\n| `s.packsOpen`, `s.packPick` | starter-pack dialog, picks | UI → Core | library intent | transient | kept |\n| `s.ncOpen`, `s.ncName`, `s.ncPid`, `s.ncInput`, `s.ncDir` | new-case dialog fields | UI → Core | `createCase` (existing library) | transient | kept |\n| `s.casePage`, `s.caseQ`, `s.cfil` | Test Cases paging, search, filter | UI | Test Cases screen state (keyed by context) | transient | kept |\n| `s.req`, `s.reqQ`, `s.fmt`, `s.rtab`, `s.rsub` | API Client request, search, body format, response tab, sub-tab | UI | workbench store | transient | kept |\n| `s.quiz` | Academy quiz state | **Dropped** | hosted Academy owns it (P19) | — | dropped |\n| `s.convoHint` | ended-conversation hint | UI | harness store; cleared by any navigation; its opening question is the core's `opening` (the conversation's, or the opened saved record's), never the title (P51) | transient | kept |\n| (none; DESIGN-V2 §3) | \"Show the calls\" preference and panel | Core | `ShellSnapshot.showCalls` (the operator's choice once made, else on until onboarding completes) and `ShellSnapshot.calls` (the active tenant's calls this app run: request line, credential kind, header names, status, duration; never a value, query or body) (P54) | preference persisted; calls in memory for the app run | added |\n| `ts.activeCase` hand-off | the case opened in the Playground | UI → Core | shell store `playground` (tenant, case, fields) → Runtime Playground prefill; the scan names the case (`scan.case`) and the core records its result (P55, P56) | until the next hand-off | kept |\n\n## R2App — per-tenant (`ts.*`)\n\n| Prototype key | Meaning | Owner | Where | Lifetime | Disposition |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `ts.reading`, `ts.reads`, `ts.firstRead`, `ts.lastRead`, `ts.warnCleared`, `ts.capsScan` | read in progress, count, first read done, last-read time, warning cleared, scan capability | Core | `ReadStatus` scope, from the tenant's read record (one per opened tenant, kept across a switch round trip, P37) | session, per tenant | kept (I4); `reads` count is not shown and never feeds a timestamp |\n| `ts.ack`, `ts.snoozed` | acknowledgments, snoozes with return | Core | `InboxEntry.hold` (`acknowledge`, or `snooze` with `returnsAt` computed in the core); intents `acknowledgeItem`/`snoozeItem`/`unsnoozeItem`; the last snooze's `SnoozeReceipt` on the Inbox scope is what the toast announces, once (P38) | session, per tenant (as v1's holds) | kept (I11); not persisted across a relaunch, as the retained holds were not |\n| `ts.prompt`, `ts.dir`, `ts.profile`, `ts.model`, `ts.app`, `ts.kind`, `ts.scanned`, `ts.scanDir`, `ts.scanProfile`, `ts.results`, `ts.activeCase`, `ts.activeInput`, `ts.activeDir` | Playground prompt, direction, profile, model, app, classified kind, scanned flag, scan selectors, per-case results, active case | prompt/dir/profile/model/app: UI; scan result + per-case results: Core | workbench store; `ScanRecordView` (existing) and library case results | prompt transient; results persisted per tenant | kept; verdict computed by the existing scan path, never by a UI classifier (the prototype's `classify` is fixture-only) |\n| `ts.extraCases`, `ts.packs` | user-created cases, packs | Core | library | persisted | kept |\n| `ts.hist` | API responses | Core | workbench history | persisted | kept (I5) |\n| `ts.topicRev`, `ts.topicDesc`, `ts.injApplied`, `ts.aesApplied`, `ts.aesRev` | applied review results | Core | read back from the product scopes after apply | — | kept for Runtime topics; `aes*` **dropped** (P18) |\n| `ts.keyRotated`, `ts.keySecretClosed`, `ts.keyDeployed`, `ts.keyDoneAt` | rotation stage | Core | `Tenant.rotations` → `ShellSnapshot.rotations: RotationView{stage, oldKey, newKey, issuedBy, deploymentAcknowledgedAt, oldKeyRemovedAt, removalRejected}`; stage derived (issuanceUnconfirmed, issued, resumed, acknowledged, removalUnconfirmed, complete); intent `acknowledgeDeployment` | per tenant, persisted (timestamps stored once, and the reviewed key name that alone confirms an unconfirmed issuance); the held secret only on its change result, for its context | **changed** (P20, P41): supported Version → Delete sequence; see screens/reviews-administration.md |\n| `ts.follows` | follow-up status per conversation | Core | sessions | persisted | kept |\n| `ts.convo`, `ts.userConvos`, `ts.msgsBy`, `ts.decs`, `ts.ended`, `ts.archived` | current conversation, user conversations, messages, decisions, ended flags, archives | Core | existing harness sessions and decisions | persisted, protected | kept |\n| `ts.draft` | composer draft | UI | shell store per tenant and workspace ID (`harnessDrafts`), with kept messages (`harnessUnsent`: not sent, or not confirmed until their own conversation reports the core took their send ID, `ConversationView.submissions`) | transient | kept |\n\n## Credential entry paths (native)\n\n| Credential | Entry | Storage | Readable by the web layer |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Scan API key | webview password field read through a ref, cleared at once, sent once as `EnteredSecret` inside `configureScanCredential` (P25) | vault (`cr-` record), Keychain v2 namespace | state and mode only (`ScanView`), never the value |\n| Management client secret | same path, `configureManagementCredential` (optional section) | vault | client id and state only |\n| Gateway workspace key | same path, `configureInferenceCredential` | vault | state only |\n| Issued API key (rotation) | `RevealSecret` host sheet / host clipboard | held per result for the active context, never persisted; retired by the review's exit (`DiscardChange` on the applied review, also before the change settles), by acknowledging the deployment, or by a context change | never |\n# Inbox and reads\n\nSource: `R2App` (`ITEMS`, `visibleItems`, `ack`, `snoozed`, `snooze`,\n`inboxRows`, `sel`, `startRead`, `recheck`, `toGo`). Chunk: C30.\n\n## Inbox\n\n- Tabs All / Needs action / Updates / Snoozed with counts. Rows: severity\n  (colour + icon + word), title, product, source line (\"API keys · cached\",\n  \"rotated 07:46\"), when, acknowledged mark. Selecting opens the detail pane:\n  body, facts table, \"Why this matters\" explanation, action button (navigates\n  with context), Acknowledge / Mark as needing action, Snooze or Unsnooze.\n- Empty states distinguish \"first read pending\" from \"nothing needs action\"\n  and name partial sources (\"3 of 6 sources were read at 07:45\").\n- Snooze: per item, core-computed return time, 24 hours for every item in\n  P09 (the prototype's deadline-bound rotation snooze is not carried: no\n  admitted operation has a grace deadline, P20). The label, toast and\n  Snoozed-tab \"Returns …\" text all state the same time (I11). The\n  `deadline` field stays optional for a future item that has a real one.\n- Contextual navigation: an item's action carries a target (screen, product,\n  tab, conversation). Into an ended conversation it sets a transient hint\n  offering \"Open the saved transcript\" and \"Start a new investigation\".\n\n## Reads (I4)\n\n- `readTenant` runs a finite read of every selected product; `ReadStatus`\n  carries per-product state (pending, ok, partial, needsRole), last-read\n  time and counts. First read on a fresh tenant shows pending everywhere.\n- Completion toast: ok \"Read finished at 07:45 · all sources complete\" or\n  warn \"· 3 sources partial\"; for fresh tenants \"· 1 product still needs a\n  role\" or \"· no activity yet in <tenant>\". `recheckProduct` after a role is\n  granted shows an info toast and re-reads.\n\n## Core contract\n\n- Scope `InboxItem{id, kind, severity, title, product, source, when, body,\n  facts, action_target, explanation, deadline?, snooze_return?, acknowledged}`\n  per tenant; intents `acknowledgeItem`, `snoozeItem`, `unsnoozeItem`,\n  `readTenant`, `recheckProduct`.\n- The rotation reminder (`rotation-<application>`) is a distinct item id from\n  the expiry alert and clears only when the old key's deletion is read back\n  (I7). Items exist only for admitted products (DESIGN-V2 §6).\n\n## Fixtures and tests\n\n- Board R2Inbox. Tests V2-R02, R04, R08, R09; V2-T04, T12, T13; V2-N02.\n# Shell, Home, tenant switcher, palette, toasts\n\nSource: `prototype/R2App.dc.html` (sidebar markup, `nav`, `switchPatch`,\n`requestSwitch`, `palette*`, `toast*`, `top`, Home section). Chunk: C28 (shell,\nHome skeleton), C30 (Home attention list backed by Inbox scope).\n\n## Sidebar\n\n- Top: tenant switcher button showing tenant name and environment pill;\n  ⌘T opens the list. Entries: every tenant (name, environment, TSG), then\n  \"Add a tenant…\". Selected tenant uses `sel/selInk`.\n- Destinations in the order of DESIGN-V2 §5 with icon, label, shortcut hint.\n  Unavailable destinations render disabled with their availability reason as\n  a tooltip and accessible description, never hidden.\n- Bottom: appearance toggle (light/dark/system) and \"Show the calls\" toggle,\n  both dispatching their Rust preference.\n- Collapses to icons below 1280px window width.\n\n## Home\n\n- Title \"Home\" with the tenant name and environment beneath; last-read line\n  from `ReadStatus` (\"Read finished at 07:45 · all sources complete\" or\n  \"· 3 sources partial\", warn-styled when partial; \"First read pending\" on a\n  fresh tenant).\n- \"Needs attention\": up to five Inbox items of kind Needs action, each with\n  severity (colour + icon + word), title, product, action button that\n  navigates with context, Acknowledge, and Snooze whose tooltip and\n  accessible name are the item's `snoozeLabel`.\n- Product cards for admitted, licensed products with their read state;\n  unlicensed products are listed once as \"Not licensed in this tenant\" and\n  unavailable products once as \"Not available in this release\" (DESIGN-V2\n  §6), never hidden.\n- Playground card (Runtime Security scan): prompt, direction, profile select,\n  verdict panel (word + icon + reason + plain explanation). Verdicts are\n  profile-aware: a detector not enabled, or a topic not assigned, reads \"Not\n  detected\" with the reason; monitor-only turns Blocked into Flagged with the\n  profile named.\n\n## Tenant switch (I1, I2)\n\n- `switchTenant{tenant_id, resolution?}`; the core refuses with\n  `SwitchBlocked{pending: {conversation, decision}}` when a Harness decision is\n  pending. The UI renders the guard dialog (Archive and switch / Discard and\n  switch / Stay) from that payload and re-dispatches with `resolution`. Initial\n  focus is on Stay, the safe default (Enter on arrival never ends the\n  conversation); Archive and switch stays the visually primary action.\n- Every entry point (switcher, palette, menu, wizard completion) uses the same\n  intent. After a switch the new tenant's Home renders from cached scopes within\n  100 ms with read status pending until the read lands.\n\n## Command palette\n\n- ⌘K. Entries: destinations from the Rust inventory, tenants, and three actions\n  (Navigate, Switch tenant, Read now). Typing filters; Enter dispatches; Escape\n  closes and restores focus. Native menu navigation while the palette is open\n  closes it first.\n\n## Toasts (I10)\n\n- Kinds ok, info, warn with icon and colour; one visible at a time, newest\n  replaces; 6 s expiry (persist under Reduce Motion); optional Undo action\n  (snooze). A toast never carries information absent from an observed scope.\n\n## Modals (I8)\n\n- Stack order kept in the shell store; only the topmost is interactive;\n  siblings get `aria-hidden`; Escape closes the topmost; focus returns to the\n  opener. Detail sheets (transcripts, facts) are modals in this stack.\n\n## Fixtures and tests\n\n- Fixture boards: R2Palette, R2Tenants, R2Dark, R2App default.\n- V2-T01, T02, T09, T10, T11; V2-N01, N03, N04, N05.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat docs/planning/WORF-START-HERE.md docs/planning/status.md docs/architecture/ui-v2/provenance.md docs/architecture/ui-v2/screens/boards.md docs/planning/chunks/C28.md'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat docs/planning/WORF-START-HERE.md docs/planning/status.md docs/architecture/ui-v2/provenance.md docs/architecture/ui-v2/screens/boards.md docs/planning/chunks/C28.md'","aggregated_output":"# Continue the current desktop work in the Worf VM\n\nThis is the 2026-11-01 continuation guide. It supersedes the old sibling\n`p09-queue/handoff` instructions about Geordi, rsync and the older C44 worktree.\nThe target is the existing macOS VM on **Worf**. Kirk's local Tart VM `airs`\nwas only a bootstrap experiment; it produced no passing P09 native acceptance.\nIts Python permission prompt is not a prerequisite for this Git migration.\n\n## Get the current source\n\nFrom an empty development directory in the Worf VM:\n\n```sh\ngit clone --branch main ssh://git@git-ssh.cdot.io/cdot/prisma-airs-desktop-v2.git\ncd prisma-airs-desktop-v2\ngit lfs install --local\ngit lfs pull\npython3 -I tools/p09/verify-migration.py\ngit rev-parse HEAD origin/main\n```\n\nFor an existing clean clone, use `git fetch origin`, `git switch main`,\n`git pull --ff-only origin main`, then `git lfs pull` and the same verification.\nPreserve local modifications before changing an existing checkout.\nThe verification checks the latest application/tooling source, all 221 previously\npending main files, every retained worktree file mapping, required commit ancestry\nand the historical L19 executable. It intentionally describes this migration\ncheckpoint; later intentional implementation changes will change its hashes.\n\nAll chunk branch tips are retained as remote branches. C37/C39/C39b/C40/C41/\nC42/C43/C44 were already merged. The C29 live and C44 scope commits were applied\nas equivalent cherry-picks. The older `p09-merge` history and detached dry merge\nare preserved as refs rather than replacing the newer integrated source.\nThe audit and exact file mapping are in\n[worktree-preservation/2026-11-01](worktree-preservation/2026-11-01/README.md).\nNo original worktree was deleted or reset.\n\n## Prepare build inputs\n\nUse macOS Apple Silicon with a logged-in GUI account and Xcode Command Line\nTools/Swift. The contracted toolchain is Rust **1.99.0** (rustfmt, clippy,\n`aarch64-apple-darwin`), Node **24.21.0** in its NVM directory, pnpm **10.6.5**,\nPython 3, and Git LFS. Install those in the VM before running the following:\n\n```sh\nmkdir -p .tools/bin\ncorepack enable pnpm --install-directory .tools/bin\nexport PATH=\"$PWD/.tools/bin:$HOME/.cargo/bin:$HOME/.nvm/versions/node/v24.21.0/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin\"\ncargo fetch --locked\ngit clone --branch v2/desktop-presentation ssh://git@git-ssh.cdot.io/cdot.io/ai-security-academy.git ../ai-security-academy\ncargo run --locked -p xtask -- fetch-inputs --source ../ai-security-academy\ncargo run --locked -p xtask -- shared-prepare --input .inputs/academy --scratch .work/academy\npnpm install --frozen-lockfile --ignore-scripts\npnpm --dir .work/academy install --frozen-lockfile --ignore-scripts\ncargo run --locked -p xtask -- shared-lifecycle --allowlist docs/architecture/shared-lifecycle.json --scratch .work/academy\npnpm --dir .work/academy exec playwright install chromium --only-shell\n```\n\n`fetch-inputs` uses the locked Academy commit **532809aa4bb2e1484e11ca9f7a414328260c7901**,\nnot the evolving branch tip. Keep the input lock unchanged for the move.\nThe Rust SCM SDK is the locked crates.io dependency; the Harness is the pinned\nrepository LFS archive. Neither needs an external source worktree. Recreate\nbuild/dependency directories here; do not restore Kirk's absolute symlinks.\n\nUse **Terminal.app** as the guest GUI execution context. Resolve its actual\nAccessibility/System Events permission prompts in the VM. A 1920×1200 display\nis suitable for the native matrix. Configure the Codex CLI/model in the VM for\nfresh read-only reviews; host authentication files are not part of this transfer.\nThe owner's planning skill is preserved at `tools/p09/skills/grill-me/SKILL.md`\nand can be installed under the guest's `~/.codex/skills/grill-me/`.\n\n## Exact current standing and next work\n\n- **C44 attempt-05: 9/9/9/9/9**, no required fixes/blockers/gaps; merged. Its\n  opaque collection scope, render-time stale-editor retirement, packet isolation\n  and complete legacy-map guard are in current source.\n- **L19: actual Vulture wizard verification passed** on attempt-03 after the\n  separately approved local credential correction. The original two reads and\n  separately approved third are charged, with **no remaining live allowance**.\n  Do not repeat the live probe. Redacted receipts and the exact historical\n  executable (LFS) are retained; raw build paths/receipts/verdicts are unchanged.\n- **C29 attempt-07: 9/9/9/8/8**, no blockers, accepted under D034 with R1/R2/E1/E2.\n  Commit `03e572be` restores Gateway/key setup, rejected/fixed/stale verification,\n  keyed Cancel/Keychain cleanup, relaunch/import/confinement checks and the full\n  **24-behavior, 48-row** wizard matrix. Syntax and completeness-map checks pass.\n  The new native flow has **not** passed yet.\n- **P09 check attempt-02: all 18 checks passed** on unchanged inputs (541 frontend\n  tests, 15 live-scope tests, 57 synthetic live-run tests, four L19 driver tests).\n  Those records are Kirk history. The current app/build inputs match those tested\n  bytes, including the owner work now committed for this move.\n- C30/C31/C32 still need their predecessor-dependent re-reviews after C29 reaches\n  full 9. The P09 phase review follows full native/check/member completion.\n\nArchive the retained Kirk P09 preparation/incomplete native generation in a new\nhistory directory before creating the Worf generation. Keep all verdict folders\nimmutable and choose fresh check/review attempt IDs. Then run:\n\n```sh\ncargo run --locked -p xtask -- native-prepare --phase P09 --target aarch64-apple-darwin --features test-fixtures\npython3 -I docs/planning/evidence/P09/native-controller/run-p09-native.py c36\npython3 -I docs/planning/evidence/P09/native-controller/run-p09-native.py c43\n```\n\nC36 proves the guest driver context; C43 proves the restored C29 native coverage.\nContinue the other required drivers serially using the retained native controller\nplan and assertion requirements. Every record must bind the newly prepared\nexecutable. C44's cumulative driver runs last. Historical C24-N06 and C31-N01/N04\naggregates remain superseded as the map states; their old raw failures are not\nrewritten or counted as passing checks.\n\nUse a fresh P09 check attempt (next currently `attempt-03`) and the portable\nhelpers in [tools/p09](../../tools/p09/README.md) for C29 attempt-08, then C30,\nC31 and C32 in order. Report every actual score and apply D034's 8-then-9 rule.\nThe copied phase packet builder is explicitly a disabled draft; finish its\ncurrent-P09 native/predecessor verification before using it for the phase review.\nC26 still requires the documented manual review fallback; do not manufacture\ncontroller completion.\n\nAfter the P09 phase passes at 9, execute the owner-approved\n[C45/P10 brief](C45-draft.md): Prisma AIRS Desktop, version 1.0.0,\n`io.cdot.airs-desktop` / `.fixture`, fresh setup with no alpha/v2 migration,\nlegacy/variant/import cleanup, chunk 8→9 and phase 9. C45 has not started.\nThe preserved pending 2.0.0 version/release work is superseded at that later\nchunk, not silently renamed during migration. October C26 installed/signing\nrecords and `docs/release/2.0.0.md` are historical/draft; pushing source neither\npublishes a release nor clears their remaining gates.\n\nPrivate live manifests, Keychains, CLI tenant TOMLs, signing keys and authentication\nprofiles stay outside Git. They are not needed for the next fixture gates.\n# Current state\n\nG00 and G01 passed (historical Claude reviews). C01–C04 and the P01 cumulative review completed on\n2026-10-17; C05–C07 and the P02 cumulative review completed on 2026-10-18;\nC08–C12 and the P03 cumulative review completed on 2026-10-19; C13–C15 and\nthe P04 cumulative review completed on 2026-10-20; C16–C18 and the P05\ncumulative review completed on 2026-10-21; C19–C22 and the P06 cumulative\nreview completed on 2026-10-23; C23–C24 and the P07 cumulative review\ncompleted on 2026-10-24. P08/C26 remains open; the owner-authorized P09\nintegration is now at fresh Worf cumulative native qualification after C44 full-9 closure.\nWorf native generation 01 passed all 19 mapped drivers with C44 last, including\nC43's 24 behaviors and 48 rows. It is preserved complete with the exact executable\nunder `evidence/P09/native-history/Worf-generation-01-complete-20261101`.\nFresh check attempt-03 passed 17/18 checks but failed import test relaunch/timing\nassertions on all three fixture runs. The corrected harness uses the production\nshutdown hook, a durable receipt boundary and a read-only fixture observer of the\narmed cut; the full import suite now passes 23/23 with every assertion retained.\nNative generation 02 is rebuilt with an exact before/after input seal; C36 passed,\nand all remaining mapped drivers will repeat before\nfresh checks and C29–C32/P09 reviews. C24-N06 and C31-N01/N04 remain superseded raw\nfailures under the unchanged map. No current native or review pass is transferred\nto changed inputs.\nUse [WORF-START-HERE](WORF-START-HERE.md) for the 2026-11-01 checkpoint and next commands. D026 (2026-10-17) makes Codex the independent reviewer of every chunk\nand of a cumulative review after every phase, each requiring at least 9 in all\nfive dimensions with empty required fixes, blockers and evidence gaps. D034 (2026-10-18, owner rule) lets a chunk complete at 8/10 with no\nblockers; each phase review still needs 9/10, after every chunk accepted below\n9 is raised to a passing review.\n\n| Gate/chunk | State | Evidence/next action |\n|---|---|---|\n| G00 | Passed (historical) 