{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_49","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'choose_setup_products|products.is_empty|RuntimeSecurity|selected products' crates/desktop-core/src/authority/setup_domain.rs | head -35; sed -n '235,300p' crates/desktop-core/src/authority/setup_domain.rs; sed -n '3427,3548p' crates/desktop-core/src/authority.rs; rg -n 'authority|intent_allowed|allowed_intent|operator_only' crates/desktop-core/src/policy.rs crates/desktop-core/src/*.rs | head -35; cat docs/planning/reviews/C30/remediation-attempt-08.md\"","aggregated_output":"85:        ProductId::RuntimeSecurity => &[CaseProduct::RuntimeSecurity],\n94:        ProductId::RuntimeSecurity => \"AI Runtime Security\",\n102:    product != ProductId::RuntimeSecurity\n133:    let mut chosen = vec![ProductId::RuntimeSecurity];\n205:            products: vec![ProductId::RuntimeSecurity],\n300:    pub(super) fn choose_setup_products(\n400:                product: Some(ProductId::RuntimeSecurity),\n441:                product: Some(ProductId::RuntimeSecurity),\n472:                ProductId::RuntimeSecurity => continue,\n        }\n    }\n\n    /// A tenant was committed outside the setup (the legacy Create tenant\n    /// or a v1 import during first run): a first-run draft is over, since\n    /// the desktop now has a tenant and the shell takes over. Its Keychain\n    /// records go to the cleanup queue; returned session records are the\n    /// caller's to delete.\n    pub(super) fn end_first_run_setup(&mut self) -> Vec<RecordId> {\n        if self\n            .data\n            .setup\n            .as_ref()\n            .is_none_or(|s| s.mode != SetupMode::FirstRun)\n        {\n            return Vec::new();\n        }\n        let context = self.data.setup.as_ref().map(|s| s.context.clone());\n        match context {\n            Some(context) => self.discard_setup(&context).unwrap_or_default(),\n            None => Vec::new(),\n        }\n    }\n\n    /// Changes the draft's profile. A new destination retires credentials\n    /// bound to the old one (returned session records are the caller's to\n    /// delete); verification results go stale through the signature.\n    pub(super) fn update_setup(\n        &mut self,\n        context: &ContextRef,\n        profile: ProfileDraft,\n    ) -> Result<Vec<RecordId>, Refusal> {\n        let profile = profile.validate().ok_or(Refusal::InvalidInput)?;\n        let setup = self.setup_for(context)?;\n        let id = setup.tenant.profile.id.clone();\n        let destination_changed = setup.tenant.profile.destination != profile.destination;\n        let tsg_changed = setup.tenant.profile.tsg_id != profile.tsg_id;\n        let mut retired = Vec::new();\n        if destination_changed {\n            for class in [\n                CredentialClass::Scan,\n                CredentialClass::Management,\n                CredentialClass::Inference,\n            ] {\n                retired.extend(self.retire_class(&id, class));\n            }\n        } else if tsg_changed {\n            retired.extend(self.retire_class(&id, CredentialClass::Management));\n        }\n        let setup = self.setup_for_mut(context)?;\n        let changed = setup.tenant.profile.label != profile.label\n            || setup.tenant.profile.tsg_id != profile.tsg_id\n            || setup.tenant.profile.destination != profile.destination\n            || setup.tenant.profile.environment != profile.environment;\n        setup.tenant.profile.label = profile.label;\n        setup.tenant.profile.tsg_id = profile.tsg_id;\n        setup.tenant.profile.destination = profile.destination;\n        setup.tenant.profile.environment = profile.environment;\n        if changed {\n            self.reissue_setup_context();\n        }\n        Ok(retired)\n    }\n\n    /// Records the chosen products (Runtime Security always, in first place).\n    pub(super) fn choose_setup_products(\n    principal: Principal,\n    inner: Arc<Inner>,\n}\n\nimpl AuthorityHandle {\n    pub fn principal(&self) -> Principal {\n        self.principal\n    }\n\n    /// Registers a new delivery session for this principal, retiring the\n    /// previous one (for example after a renderer reload).\n    pub fn register_delivery_session(&self) -> Result<DeliverySession, Refusal> {\n        lock(&self.inner)?.operator_sessions.register()\n    }\n\n    /// Admits or refuses one delivered Intent. Admission never awaits remote\n    /// IO, Keychain calls or an operator answer while holding the state.\n    pub async fn dispatch(&self, delivery: Delivery, intent: Intent) -> Result<Receipt, Refusal> {\n        let kind = intent.kind();\n        let (result, effects) = {\n            let mut state = lock(&self.inner)?;\n            let digest = intent_digest(&state.salt, &intent);\n            match state.operator_sessions.check(&delivery, &digest) {\n                Admit::Refused(refusal) => return Err(refusal),\n                Admit::Duplicate(result) => return result,\n                Admit::Fresh => {\n                    let mut effects = Vec::new();\n                    // What an import writes waits while it (or its\n                    // rollback) runs, until every receipt has settled, and\n                    // while a receipt cannot be read (D050).\n                    let result =\n                        if state.v1_import_holds() && import_v1_domain::waits_for_import(&intent) {\n                            Err(Refusal::Busy)\n                        } else {\n                            admit(\n                                &mut state,\n                                &self.inner.session,\n                                &self.inner.adapters,\n                                intent,\n                                &mut effects,\n                            )\n                        };\n                    if result.is_err() {\n                        effects.clear();\n                    }\n                    // Settlements published by this intent are kept on\n                    // this Mac whether or not the intent itself succeeded.\n                    effects.extend(gateway_local_effects(&mut state));\n                    // Learner records wait in the ledger for a confirmed\n                    // save; once one has happened, let cleanup resume.\n                    if !state.durability_unconfirmed && !state.data.learner_cleanup.is_empty() {\n                        effects.push(Effect::Cleanup);\n                    }\n                    state\n                        .operator_sessions\n                        .record(&delivery, digest, result.clone());\n                    (result, effects)\n                }\n            }\n        };\n        run_effects(&self.inner, effects);\n        // Only the request's kind and the refusal's code (D051).\n        self.inner\n            .diagnostics\n            .record(crate::diagnostics::Event::Intent {\n                kind: kind.to_owned(),\n                refusal: result.as_ref().err().map(refusal_code),\n            });\n        result\n    }\n\n    /// Returns the current redacted snapshot and subscribes to its updates\n    /// atomically, so no update between them is lost.\n    pub fn observe(&self, scope: ViewScope) -> Result<Observation, Refusal> {\n        let mut state = lock(&self.inner)?;\n        match scope {\n            ViewScope::Shell => {\n                let snapshot = state.snapshot();\n                let updates = state.subscribers.subscribe().ok_or(Refusal::Busy)?;\n                Ok(Observation::Shell { snapshot, updates })\n            }\n            ViewScope::AcademyCall(operation) => Ok(Observation::AcademyCall(\n                state.observe_academy_call(&operation)?,\n            )),\n            ViewScope::Management(operation) => Ok(Observation::Management(\n                state.observe_management(&operation)?,\n            )),\n            ViewScope::Workbench(operation) => {\n                Ok(Observation::Workbench(state.observe_workbench(&operation)?))\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    /// Live observers registered with the core (retired ones are pruned).\n    pub fn observer_count(&self) -> usize {\n        lock(&self.inner)\n            .map(|mut s| s.subscribers.len())\n            .unwrap_or(0)\n    }\n\n    /// Admits remote work bound to the current context. Production remote\n    /// operations (C03 Scan) are admitted through this path from their\n    /// intents; fixtures use it to exercise the shared lifecycle.\n    #[cfg(any(test, feature = \"test-fixtures\"))]\n    pub fn admit_fixture_operation(\n        &self,\n        context: &ContextRef,\n        bytes: usize,\n        work: runtime::Work,\n    ) -> Result<OperationId, Refusal> {\n        let (id, starts) = {\n            let mut state = lock(&self.inner)?;\n            state.check_context(context)?;\n            state\n                .operations\n                .admit(context.as_str(), bytes, work, Instant::now())?\n        };\n        run_effects(&self.inner, vec![Effect::Start(starts)]);\n        Ok(id)\n    }\n\n    /// Cancels an operation admitted by this principal.\nrg: crates/desktop-core/src/policy.rs: No such file or directory (os error 2)\ncrates/desktop-core/src/gateway.rs:1175:            \"authority\",\ncrates/desktop-core/src/fixtures.rs:10:use crate::authority::{Adapters, CredentialStore, ImportFile, ImportPicker};\ncrates/desktop-core/src/fixtures.rs:562:    requests: Vec<(u64, crate::authority::ConfirmationRequest)>,\ncrates/desktop-core/src/fixtures.rs:584:    pub fn requests(&self) -> Vec<(u64, crate::authority::ConfirmationRequest)> {\ncrates/desktop-core/src/fixtures.rs:603:impl crate::authority::OperatorConfirmation for ScriptedConfirmer {\ncrates/desktop-core/src/fixtures.rs:607:        request: crate::authority::ConfirmationRequest,\ncrates/desktop-core/src/fixtures.rs:649:impl crate::authority::SecretPresenter for ScriptedSecrets {\ncrates/desktop-core/src/fixtures.rs:692:impl crate::authority::FileSaver for ScriptedSaver {\ncrates/desktop-core/src/features.rs:159:    pub workspace: Option<crate::authority::SelectedWorkspace>,\ncrates/desktop-core/src/diagnostics.rs:92:        use crate::authority::{\ncrates/desktop-core/src/wire.rs:5://! non-canonical sequence numbers are rejected before any authority is\ncrates/desktop-core/src/wire.rs:15:use crate::authority::{Intent, Receipt, Refusal, ShellSnapshot};\ncrates/desktop-core/src/wire.rs:165:/// Why a request was rejected before reaching authority.\ncrates/desktop-core/src/wire.rs:247:    crate::authority::SwitchBlocked::export_all(&config)?;\ncrates/desktop-core/src/wire.rs:248:    crate::authority::PendingDecisionRef::export_all(&config)?;\ncrates/desktop-core/src/delivery.rs:11:use crate::authority::{Receipt, Refusal};\ncrates/desktop-core/src/lib.rs:3://! The core owns native authority: callers hold a principal-bound\ncrates/desktop-core/src/lib.rs:11:mod authority;\ncrates/desktop-core/src/lib.rs:47:pub use authority::{\ncrates/desktop-core/src/lib.rs:62:pub use authority::{\ncrates/desktop-core/src/management.rs:41:use crate::authority::CredentialStore;\ncrates/desktop-core/src/authority.rs:1://! Native authority: principal-bound handles, finite intents and observation.\ncrates/desktop-core/src/authority.rs:108:/// A typed request for one desktop action under the caller's authority.\ncrates/desktop-core/src/authority.rs:307:    /// Keep a Gateway change draft on this Mac (no review or authority).\ncrates/desktop-core/src/authority.rs:1460:    /// Called with the authority locked: it must not block.\ncrates/desktop-core/src/authority.rs:3007:            .expect(\"authority\");\ncrates/desktop-core/src/authority.rs:3017:            .expect(\"authority\");\ncrates/desktop-core/src/authority.rs:3062:            .expect(\"authority\");\ncrates/desktop-core/src/authority.rs:3072:            .expect(\"authority\");\ncrates/desktop-core/src/authority.rs:3105:            .expect(\"authority\");\ncrates/desktop-core/src/observe.rs:3://! Observers never apply backpressure to authority. When a subscriber's queue\ncrates/desktop-core/src/observe.rs:11:use crate::authority::ShellSnapshot;\ncrates/desktop-core/src/sessions.rs:831:    /// authority locked.)\ncrates/desktop-core/src/gateway_local.rs:8://! review, Apply authority, a reply or a one-time key, so nothing here can\ncrates/desktop-core/src/runtime.rs:3://! The registry lives inside the authority state, so context retirement,\n# C30 remediation after attempt-08 (9/8/9/8/8, fail)\n\n| Finding | Remediation | Where |\n|---|---|---|\n| R1 a snoozed update's expiry not published at its deadline | The overview's time signature (`OverviewSignature`) now includes the holds in effect (acknowledgments, and snoozes whose return time has not passed) besides freshness, the face and the attention ids, so the deadline ticker publishes when any snooze ends, actionable or not, even while the read is already stale. Test: `ui_v2_inbox::a_snoozed_update_returns_at_its_deadline_and_is_published` (a normal Runtime activity update snoozed; the stale update drained from the production Shell subscription; the clock moved past the return time with no intent or read; the published snapshot shows the hold gone) | `observation_domain.rs`, `authority.rs` |\n\nB1/E1 (the C29 live Vulture verification receipt) stay owner-gated (`evidence/C29/live-scope-request.md`).\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
