{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_50","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '/## D058/,/## Directions explicitly requested/p' docs/planning/decisions.md; sed -n '/## D060/,\"'$p'\"' docs/planning/decisions.md; cat docs/planning/chunks/C29.md; cat docs/planning/reviews/C30/attempt-10/invocation.json\"","aggregated_output":"## D058 — UI v2 \"Refined Native\": frozen prototype, P09 extraction plan\n\nAccepted by the owner on 2026-10-26 (\"I accept it as written\"), with authority to implement P09 end to end autonomously and to proceed with C28 while C26 remains in progress; every chunk is reviewed until it scores 9 in every dimension.\n\nThe owner explored fifteen interactive shell concepts on a Claude Design canvas\n(https://claude.ai/artifact/2SEXT1XMHdZkxHvdw8oaYL), selected \"Refined\nNative\", and iterated its prototype (R2App, R2Onboard, R2Harness ×3,\nR2Rationale) through sixteen independent Codex usability reviews (scores 6, 7,\n7, then 8 on rounds 4–16). The prototype is frozen at canvas version 134 and\ncopied verbatim into `docs/architecture/ui-v2/prototype/` with a SHA-256\nmanifest; the canvas page is not changed again. Prototype data is invented and\nis never shipped.\n\nDecisions (grilling session, 55 questions, all recommendations accepted):\n\n1. Extraction is spec, then TypeScript presentation, then Rust contract, as\n   phase P09 chunks C27–C34 (see the chunk index). The first implementation\n   slice is the shell plus the first-run wizard and add-tenant sheet.\n2. The prototype's state model is normative for twelve named invariants\n   (`docs/architecture/ui-v2/invariants.md`) and illustrative for code shape.\n   Every prototype state field is assigned Rust-owned/observed or UI-transient\n   (`state-ownership.md`); nothing goes to browser storage.\n3. D014 holds: secrets enter only through the host secret sheet and vault;\n   an issued API key is disclosed only through the existing `RevealSecret`\n   host path, held for the active context and never persisted; key rotation\n   is the admitted sequence additional key (`Version`) → local deployment\n   acknowledgement → old key `Delete` with readback (no invented grace\n   period or revocation); typed-name confirmation is validated in the core;\n   tenant switch is refused by the core while a Harness decision is pending;\n   write-capable tool calls use the native confirmation sheet.\n3a. Only products with an admitted service are verified, inventoried or\n   changed (Runtime Security, Gateway, Red Team and Model/skill reads).\n   Agentic Identity Security and Agentic Endpoint Security render as \"Not\n   available in this release\" with a dependency gate; no inventory,\n   verification result or mutation is invented for them.\n4. Tokens live in a local `--v2-*` file; Academy variables stay for the\n   embedded learner view. One Rust navigation inventory feeds the native menu,\n   sidebar and palette; ⌘1–⌘9 are menu-defined. Feature ids gain `home` and\n   `inbox`.\n5. The new shell ships behind a Rust-owned `ui_variant` flag and the legacy\n   shell, flag and legacy acceptance scripts are removed in C34. The Academy\n   learner view is embedded unchanged.\n6. The wizard realises D013 (scan key first and only required credential);\n   v1 import is offered on the tenant step.\n7. Verification: Vitest fixtures named after every prototype wrapper board,\n   Rust tests per invariant, native acceptance extended with focus ring, live\n   regions, topmost modal and Reduce Motion persistence, screenshot evidence\n   at 100%/200% in both themes per chunk. Live calls only in C29 (verify,\n   Vulture, reads) and C31 (review apply, Redtail, prefixed) inside the scope\n   designated 2026-10-25. C27 is reviewed at 9/10 in every dimension and the\n   controller enforces it: a `docs_only` chunk has no native preparation or\n   acceptance and refuses owner acceptance at completion and at recognition;\n   C28–C34 follow D034.\n8. Minimum window 1180×720 with the rail collapsing below 1280 wide; toasts\n   persist under Reduce Motion; \"Show the calls\" panel shows diagnostics-\n   redacted wire data; English only in P09; chunks commit on main except C34.\n9. C27 proceeds in parallel with C26 (docs and controller registration only);\n   C28 waits for C26.\n\n\n## D059 — P09 re-cut: port the prototype, one gate per screen at 8\n\nAccepted by the owner on 2026-10-29 after a grilling session (23 questions, all\naccepted; `docs/planning/p09-recut.md`). C32 had taken twenty review rounds\nwhile the built v2 screens never matched the design: chunks had wrapped the\nlegacy feature components in v2 frames instead of porting the prototype.\n\n- The frozen prototype (D058, version 134) is the specification per screen; the\n  canvas is not consulted (it is unreachable from the implementing account).\n- A screen is done when it matches its board side by side at 1440×900 in both\n  themes with real core data, judged by the owner from composites kept under\n  the chunk's evidence; parity is structural (regions, widths, spacing, type\n  scale, tokens, component shapes), content differs, accessibility\n  corrections may deviate and are noted. Parity precedes review.\n- One heavy gate per chunk after that approval (rebuild, native acceptance,\n  the full fixture suite, the Codex review), accepted at 8 under D032/D034; the\n  phase review stays 9 and every chunk accepted at 8 is raised in C44.\n- v2 screens import no legacy feature view; the legacy files stay for the\n  legacy shell until C44 removes it. C33 was committed without a receipt (its\n  core stands; its two screens are superseded).\n- Chunks: C35 shell, C36 Home, C37 Inbox fix-up, C38 Harness, C39 Administration\n  (a: Runtime Security, b: other products), C40 Test Cases, C41 API Client,\n  C42 Academy (prototype chrome around the hosted embed), C43 Wizard re-port\n  over the existing state machine, C44 legacy removal on a branch and the P09\n  review. C34 is superseded. `Subject::LAST_CHUNK` is 44.\n\n## Directions explicitly requested before round 1\n## D060 — No import from the alpha; this desktop is v1\n\nDecided by the owner on 2026-10-31, in the owner's words: \"i really really really don't want to have an import from v1. in fact, i plan on calling this v1 since the previous was an alpha.\"\n\n- The previous desktop (`/Users/cdot/development/cdot65/prisma-airs-desktop`) is the alpha. Nothing is imported from it: the reviewed import of alpha work (C23: the Import from v1 destination and view, the wizard's \"Used Prisma AIRS Desktop 1?\" box and the tenant step's import link, the first-run import frame) is removed from the one presentation in C44, its native checks C23-N01..N09 are retired without replacement, and the legacy-script map and the C44 cumulative set drop `acceptance_c23.py`.\n- Still to decide the same way, in a follow-up chunk the owner names (proposed C45): the core's alpha-import intents and reader (`import_v1_domain`, the `V1Import*` intents, the host adapters), Settings' file-based \"Import tenant profiles\" and the API Client's \"Import v1 API Client profile\" adoption, which are alpha-import surfaces too; their removal changes contracts and earlier chunks' tests and is not done inside the P09 closure.\n- Naming: this desktop becomes v1 and the previous one the alpha. The rename touches the application identity that lets the two coexist (bundle identifiers, data roots, Keychain namespaces, D001-era identities) and the whole document set; it is its own chunk after P09, not a find-and-replace.\n- The product name shown today stays \"Prisma AIRS Desktop v2\" until that chunk.\n\n# C29 — First-run wizard and add-tenant sheet\n\nPhase: P09. Status: planned. Required predecessor: C28.\n\n## Outcome\n\nA first-run user is taken from welcome to a verified tenant with credentials in the vault, selected products, optional starter packs and optional Academy account; an existing user adds a tenant through the same component in add mode. Realises D013.\n\n## Inputs and dependency gates\n\nC28; screens/wizard.md. Read the [common execution contract](../IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md),\n[review protocol](../review-protocol.md), and [test catalogue](../test-catalogue.md).\nRead the [UI v2 specification](../../architecture/ui-v2/DESIGN-V2.md) and its\ncompanions; the frozen prototype under `docs/architecture/ui-v2/prototype/` is\nan immutable input. Freeze all source/shared dependency inputs.\n\n## Milestones\n\n1. Intents `verifyTenantSetup` (streaming `VerifyStep`, using existing reads per admitted product; unavailable products report \"not available\", never a result), `completeOnboarding`, `addTenant`; scan key required, management client and Gateway optional (D013, P17); secret entry only through the host secret sheet returning vault ids; v1 import offered as a secondary action on the tenant step.\n2. Wizard component with steps, validation (`aria-invalid`, `aria-describedby`, invalidation signature), rail context line, finite \"Open Prisma AIRS\", add mode (sheet 1160×780, 244px rail, Cancel semantics).\n3. Warnings from verify become Inbox items at completion (type defined here, rendered in C30).\n4. Fixtures for every R2On* board and R2AddTenant; copy.ts for the wizard including the welcome and trust text.\n\n## Required acceptance\n\n- `onboarding` transitions needed → inProgress → done; cancel in add mode writes nothing: the draft and its credentials are discarded (P27; stronger than the leftover credential the prototype assumed).\n- No intent persists, echoes or logs a secret: per P25 (accepted in C28) a secret enters once as `EnteredSecret` from the webview field and leaves it nowhere else; the host test on the mock runtime (`setup_draft_intents_cross_ipc_without_echoing_secrets_or_creating_tenants`) shows no receipt, snapshot or Keychain call carries it.\n- Unavailable products (AIS, AES) are not selectable and never verified; V2-T19 for the products step.\n- Live: verify against the designated read-only tenant (Vulture) under the owner scope, recorded as a redacted receipt; no writes.\n- T09 for every step; V2-N02.\n\n## Evidence and completion\n\nAs C28, plus the live verify receipt.\n\n## Safety and recovery\n\nStop on any unexpected tenant or authority state. Missing live access blocks the live row; it does not pass.\n{\n  \"command_without_prompt\": [\n    \"codex\",\n    \"--no-daemon\",\n    \"-a\",\n    \"never\",\n    \"--disable\",\n    \"hooks\",\n    \"--disable\",\n    \"plugins\",\n    \"--disable\",\n    \"apps\",\n    \"--disable\",\n    \"remote_plugin\",\n    \"--disable\",\n    \"browser_use\",\n    \"--disable\",\n    \"browser_use_external\",\n    \"--disable\",\n    \"in_app_browser\",\n    \"--disable\",\n    \"computer_use\",\n    \"--disable\",\n    \"image_generation\",\n    \"--disable\",\n    \"multi_agent\",\n    \"--disable\",\n    \"skill_search\",\n    \"--disable\",\n    \"skill_mcp_dependency_install\",\n    \"--disable\",\n    \"unbounded_connection_retries\",\n    \"exec\",\n    \"-s\",\n    \"read-only\",\n    \"--skip-git-repo-check\",\n    \"--ephemeral\",\n    \"--ignore-user-config\",\n    \"--ignore-rules\",\n    \"-m\",\n    \"gpt-6.1-sol\",\n    \"--json\",\n    \"--color\",\n    \"never\",\n    \"-c\",\n    \"web_search=\\\"disabled\\\"\",\n    \"-c\",\n    \"model_reasoning_effort=\\\"xhigh\\\"\",\n    \"--output-schema\",\n    \"docs/architecture/review-verdict.schema.json\",\n    \"-o\",\n    \"/Users/cdot/development/redtail/prisma-airs-desktop-v2-current/docs/planning/reviews/C30/attempt-10/verdict-returned.json\"\n  ],\n  \"model_requested\": \"gpt-6.1-sol\",\n  \"harness_version_observed\": \"codex-cli 0.166.0\",\n  \"request_sha256\": \"42ea9c8e74e96874f657fa11d16665cc7208430b10b2b19609d15a67101ad1dc\",\n  \"schema_sha256\": \"fa5ddc9b8371a97cdfb8055387e31916fad002859f88fc6f21340844ee2a1875\",\n  \"feature_probe_sha256\": \"bb4d01d583993c8e3c431e0437092e6c288e9b5da919595063853d37e2d89862\",\n  \"restricted_features_observed\": {\n    \"hooks\": \"false\",\n    \"plugins\": \"false\",\n    \"apps\": \"false\",\n    \"remote_plugin\": \"false\",\n    \"browser_use\": \"false\",\n    \"browser_use_external\": \"false\",\n    \"in_app_browser\": \"false\",\n    \"computer_use\": \"false\",\n    \"image_generation\": \"false\",\n    \"multi_agent\": \"false\",\n    \"skill_search\": \"false\",\n    \"skill_mcp_dependency_install\": \"false\",\n    \"unbounded_connection_retries\": \"false\"\n  },\n  \"limits\": \"CLI arguments and feature probe establish requested isolation; inspect actual run events and reviewer limitations. No provider/model authorship or review pass is inferred.\"\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
