{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_66","type":"agent_message","text":"I also found a destructive retry path. An unconfirmed “Discard and switch” intent survives tenant/context changes because it has no context binding. Retrying it makes Rust discard whichever conversation is currently pending, without checking that it is the conversation named by the original guard. I reproduced the retained retry state in memory and traced the native path. I’ll report this separately from the stale timing evidence."}}
